+
+# Request
+
+Implement JSON Pointer as specified in RFC 6901 (first of several features that build on it).
+
+Export `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` from `src/index.ts`. It returns the value the pointer refers
+to in the JSON document. It throws an error when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer, or when it
+does not resolve to a value of the document.
+
+# Acceptance criteria
+
+- `""` resolves to the whole document.
+- `/`-separated reference tokens address object members and array elements; `~1` decodes to `/` and
+  `~0` to `~` (in that order); a `~` not followed by `0` or `1` is invalid.
+- A non-empty pointer not starting with `/` is invalid.
+- Array indexes are `0` or digits without leading zero; `-` (past the end) and non-canonical indexes do
+  not resolve; out-of-range indexes do not resolve.
+- Only own members are resolved (no `__proto__`, `constructor`, inherited properties).
+- Pointers into primitives or null do not resolve; a member whose value is `null` does resolve.
